Construct the diagnosis prompt with (q, y, a∗ ); The student performs a diagnosis following the prompt's hierarchical logic: Phase 1: Check if final answer is semantically equivalent to GT⇒Format Error; Phase 2: Assess evidence sufficiency from the trajectory's [Evidence] blocks:; if evidence is sufficient to derive the GT answer then Phase 3: Locate the earliest divergent reasoning step ⇒ Reasoning Error; else Phase 4: Perform entity provenance check on each search query; if ∃ valid query with failed retrieval then Set c to Retriever Error and k† to the failed evidence block; else Set c to Search Error and k† to the first poisoned search action; if c is Format Error then Set k† ← null; Return (c, k† ) as the control signal for local repair;
```

```
switch c do case Format Error do Prompt the model with (q, y) to generate EM-valid answer variants; Return the variant list as arepaired; case Reasoning Error do Extract valid prefix yprefix ← y[1 : k†-1]; Aggregate all retrieved documents Dall(y) from the trajectory; Prompt the model with (q, yprefix, Dall(y)) to re-reason and generate answer; Return arepaired; case Retriever Error do Extract valid prefix yprefix ← y[1 : k†-1]; Extract queries whose retrieval results failed at and after k† : Qfailed; Rewrite each qi ∈ Qfailed into alternative formulations {q(1) i , q(2) i , q(3) i }; Re-retrieve: Dnew ← ⋃j R(q(j) i , top-k); Prompt the model with (q, yprefix, Dnew) to generate answer; Return arepaired; case Search Error do Extract valid prefix yprefix ← y[1 : k†-1]; Turn 0: Generate search plan from (q, yprefix); Initialize new history h ← plan; for t = 1 to T do Prompt the model with (q, yprefix, h, t, T ); Parse output: <reason> + action; if action is <search>query</search> then d ← R(query, top-k); Append reason, query, and d to h; else if action is <answer>result</answer> then Return result as arepaired; Force answer generation on final turn; Return arepaired;
```

